   "note": "Load holding fails during a slow leak at 18 degrees, so the walker is lost either way; the models differ in which actuator gives out first. Level 1 ties leg force and centre-of-pressure authority to the same capacity (A3, A4) and tips. Level 2 has CL-05's reverse-jointed legs standing on a knee bent 0.3 rad (DQ-027); its ankles keep the CoM over the foot while the legs sag, so it drops the cockpit at 3.1 m/s (HAZ-PIL-002) with the adopted torques and at any knee from 15 to 40 kN m, and tips with the ankle at 20 kN m or less."
