   "note": "A slow leak at 19.5 degrees with load holding working; both levels lock at about 2.9 s. Before the lock, level 1's centre-of-pressure limit (A3) and leg sag (A4) let its CoM drift to the foot edge, so the locked body tips (A5) at 3.4 s. Level 2 has CL-05's reverse-jointed legs standing on a knee bent 0.3 rad (DQ-027); it keeps its CoM over the foot until the lock and holds with the ankle at any torque from 15 kN m up, and tips only with the knee at 15 kN m: here level 1's assumptions, not the actuators, decide."
